Build the servlet classes against the Java 8 API, matching the bytecode
level (major 52) of upstream's own release WAR.

Upstream builds their published draw.war with JDK 8
(.github/workflows/war.yml: "Set up JDK 1.8", distribution zulu, java-version 8),
but etc/build/build.xml passes no -source/-target/--release to <javac>, so a
build with a newer JDK silently produces class files that will not load on
older servlet-container JVMs. Pin the release level so the source build stays
faithful to the release artifact regardless of the JDK used to build it.

Not submitted upstream (no PRs accepted, per README.md).

--- a/etc/build/build.xml
+++ b/etc/build/build.xml
@@ -728,7 +728,7 @@
 	-->
 	<target name="javac" description="Java compilation">
 		<mkdir dir="${javac.dir}"/>
-		<javac includeantruntime="false" srcdir="${src.dir}" destdir="${javac.dir}">
+		<javac includeantruntime="false" release="8" srcdir="${src.dir}" destdir="${javac.dir}">
 			<classpath refid="javac.class.path" />
 		</javac>
 		<copy todir="${javac.dir}" file="${src.dir}/log4j.properties" />
